the best advice I can offer.

Practice the dagger skill.  A stack of daggers will be usefull if
(when?) you run out of arrows.

If possible, bless your arrows.  They don't disappear as oftten after
hitting if they are blessed.  Higher enchantment also helps here, so I
tend try to save my +2 arrows until after I get a chance to bless them.

As for tatics:
If you are more than 2 squares in a line from a monster, fire a volley
of arrows.  If not, then retreat if you have an unobstructed line of
escape.  Do Not retreat into unexplored space, or if you left a peaceful
monster behind you.  Fire at monsters in rooms from outside the doorway
where the opportunity allows.  And once you get a good dagger/meele
weapon, don't be afraid to hit the x key and meele.  You will get mobbed
sooner or later and have to use the old wombat technique.

If you are chaotic, I wouldn't bother sacing for an artifact, as most
chaotic R's get Sting as the first gift.  If neutral, feel free.

